      "id": "berklee-music-theory-book-1-p0035",
      "source_en": "Lesson 14. Accidentals\n\nAccidentals are symbols that alter a note’s pitch.\n\nSharps 23 The sharp sign # raises a note’s pitch by a half step, the next higher note on the\n\nkeyboard. This note may be a white or a black key. (H = half step)",
